result.evidence:
Branch v2/f4 checked out detached at d9b35e7 (22 commits on master's merge base dc9873f). The tree was clean when I finished, the server on 8014 was stopped, and server/v2.db was removed.

What passed:
- `PYTHONPATH=. python3 server/checks/f4.py` ends "ok  F4 schema, traps and check-ins, days, causes, pace, estimate, prefs, access and carry". It also prints one PENDING line: app.py does not install deps.swap_middleware.
- `server/test_flow.py` prints "all good".
- `python3 server/estimate.py` prints "estimate ok". `python3 server/ratings.py` prints "ratings ok", with 121/171/163 distinct priors per tier and every level L1–L7 at 5% or more.
- Migration: I built old.db with master's code (git archive master into the scratchpad): 3 learners, 115 attempts, 67 traps including two numeric variants of one reason, 15 saved, 6 sessions, a users row. Running the branch's db.init() on a backup copy lost no row in users, sessions, practice_seen, learners, attempts or saved. Traps went 67 → 66 by norm: hits summed, owed MAX, open if either row was open, seed 42 and session from the latest wrong attempt, reason = the latest text. Every attempt got stem, offered and norm. trap_log was backfilled, handles too (a second 'Sam' gets null), and a second init took 0.00 s.
- HTTP probes on 8014:
  - a first drill answer creates the learners row;
  - retired code: GET 200, PUT /api/me 401 {retired:true, into:null}, notes 401;
  - every PUT /api/me rule I tried (prefs 422 naming the key, merge storing only non-defaults, exam_date past or impossible, X-Tz zone, rw fields, board, country, avatar, minutes, tests, handle 409/422, name);
  - activity weeks=26 gives 182 rows, weeks=54 gives 422; GET /api/prefs returns 66 keys;
  - an exact saved replay files repeat=1 and mastery stays unchanged;
  - today's challenge item: access None before and after answering and for another learner;
  - live mock item: access None; notes on it return no template;
  - record_paper takes qstate ms and conf, reads flags, and snapshots result.odds; the mock's minutes are counted once;
  - an answer at 23:30 UTC lands on the next local day with X-Tz -120;
  - /api/me/carry leaves 0 source rows in every LEARNER_TABLES table.
- satdates matches the College Board dates page, including March 6, 2027 and the anticipated 2027–28 dates. cb_percentiles.json values match College Board's SAT user percentile page (spot-checked math, rw and total).
- Nothing in the owned files contradicts decisions 1–5: no class tables, words_from has no math deck, twin challenge days are protected and carried.

`git diff --stat master...HEAD` shows 14 files. ratings.py, data/cb_percentiles.json and tools/seed_ratings.py are assigned to F4 by the upgrade files; test_flow.py is not.

Failures I reproduced myself are listed in defects.
